/*Q15. Rohan wants to send an encrypted message to his friend. To make it fun and secure, he decided to use a simple encryption algorithm.
The encryption rule is as follows:
• The Ist character of the string is repeated once,
• The 2nd character is repeated twice,
• The 3rd character is repeated three times,... and so on.
Your task is to write a Java program that applies this encryption algorithm to a given string and displays the encrypted message.
Input Format:
• A single line of input containing a string.
Output Format:
• A single string where each character is repeated based on its position in the original string.

*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class Encrypt {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        String s = sc.nextLine();
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
                sb.append(s.charAt(i));
            }
        }
        System.out.println(sb);
        sc.close();
    }
}
